---
import "../../styles/surfaces.css";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { loadCompareIndex } from "../../lib/batch3";

const page = loadCompareIndex();
const description = "ChartKit against 20 charting libraries. Every feature row is in the table, losses next to wins, with verification and source.";
---

<Base title="Compare" description={description} tone="light">
  <div class="wrap surface prose">
    <h1>Compare</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      ChartKit against {page.rivals.length} libraries, from the feature matrix. A loss is a feature the other library
      scores higher on. A win is the reverse. Unknown cells count as neither. Every scored row stays in the table.
    </p>
    <p>
      Other libraries were checked on {page.dateChecked} against types and schemas, not by rendering. A typed option can
      overstate what draws. ChartKit was rechecked on {page.chartkitRechecked} against main <code>{page.chartkitCommit}</code>.
      Radar, treemap, sankey, and funnel are native. Tooltip, zoom, and pan are native in the client runtime. The static
      SVG does not paint them. <a href="/features#method">Method</a>. <a href="/features.json">features.json</a>. Timings,
      losses included, are on <a href="/benchmarks">Benchmarks</a>. The paste converter covers Chart.js,
      Recharts, and ECharts: <a href="/convert">convert a chart</a>.
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Library</th>
            <th>Version</th>
            <th class="num">ChartKit ahead</th>
            <th class="num">ChartKit behind</th>
            <th class="num">Same</th>
            <th class="num">Unknown</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            page.rivals.map(({ library, win, loss, tie, unknown }) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">
                  <a href={`/compare/${library.id}`}>{library.name}</a>
                </th>
                <td>{library.version}</td>
                <td class="num win">{win}</td>
                <td class="num loss">{loss}</td>
                <td class="num">{tie}</td>
                <td class="num">{unknown}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
